# Date display format

All **user-visible date-only** strings must render as **`Oct 10, 2026`** — abbreviated month, day without leading zero, comma, four-digit year.

Skill: [date-display skill](../skills/date-display/SKILL.md). Locale wiring: [frontend-i18n.mdc](frontend-i18n.mdc).

## Required Intl options

```typescript
export const DISPLAY_DATE_OPTIONS: Intl.DateTimeFormatOptions = {
  year: 'numeric',
  month: 'short',
  day: 'numeric',
}
```

Pass **`getIntlLocaleTag(language)`** from `@webonone/i18n` (or a service helper that wraps it) — never bare `toLocaleDateString()` with no options or `undefined` locale.

```typescript
formatLocaleDate(value, DISPLAY_DATE_OPTIONS, i18n.language)
// → Oct 10, 2026 (en) · localized month name in si-LK with same shape
```

## Where this applies

| Surface | Rule |
|---|---|
| List row subtitles | [item-list skill](../skills/item-list/SKILL.md) |
| Details / profile fields | [details-page-cards skill](../skills/details-page-cards/SKILL.md) |
| Invoices, history, media modified dates | Same helper + options |
| Date ranges | `{start} – {end}` with each side formatted |
| AI / chat copy that cites a calendar date | Same options when rendering for humans |

**Not in scope:** API payloads and DB columns stay **ISO 8601** (`YYYY-MM-DD` or full timestamp). [form-creation skill](../skills/form-creation/SKILL.md) — `DatePicker` input state is `Date`; convert to API strings separately.

## Date + time

When a timestamp includes time, keep the **date portion** on `DISPLAY_DATE_OPTIONS` and add time fields:

```typescript
const DISPLAY_DATETIME_OPTIONS: Intl.DateTimeFormatOptions = {
  ...DISPLAY_DATE_OPTIONS,
  hour: 'numeric',
  minute: '2-digit',
}
// → Oct 10, 2026, 3:45 PM
```

Do not use a different date shape for datetime rows.

## Service helpers (reference)

| Service | Helper |
|---|---|
| All frontends | `@webonone/i18n` — `formatDisplayDate`, `formatDisplayDateTime`, `formatCalendarYmd` |
| Per-service wrapper | `<service>/frontend/src/shared/utils/formatDisplayDate.ts` — resolves `getAppI18n().language` |
| WebOnOne v2 | `@/shared/utils/formatLocaleDate.ts` — same API with `formatLocaleDate` / `formatLocaleDateTime` names |
| Payment invoices | `@/shared/utils/money.ts` → `formatDate` (delegates to `formatDisplayDate`) |
| Media browser | `formatMediaDate` in `formatMedia.ts` (delegates to `formatDisplayDateTime`) |

## Forbidden

- Raw ISO / SQL dates in UI (`2026-10-10`, `2026-10-10T…`)
- `toLocaleDateString()` with no `options` (browser-default shape drifts)
- Hard-coded `en-US` / `en-LK` in feature components when `i18n.language` is available
- `DD/MM/YYYY`, `MM/DD/YYYY`, or numeric-only month strings
- `date-fns` / `moment` display formatters that bypass the shared options

## Verification

```bash
npm run build:i18n
npm run type-check -w @webonone/<service>-frontend
```

Manual: switch **English** → row/detail date reads `Oct 10, 2026`; switch **සිංහල** → month localizes, order stays day–month–year with comma before year.
